 "notes": "Tier shelf. Old k128 (Shaver head), k129 (Clipper guard) and k130 (Shaver cleaning cartridge) merged into 'Shaver & clipper spare parts' with part types in t (spare parts kind keeps its old source). Range repeats (Braun Series, Philips OneBlade, 'Series shavers and OneBlade') removed from beard-trimmer and spare-parts kinds; each line now appears once in the kind it belongs to and in the brand register (Braun, Philips, Panasonic, Remington, Wahl, Andis). Model lists rebuilt from independent tests: TechGearLab electric razors (Braun Series 8 best overall, Series 3 ProSkin best value, Philips Norelco S9000 Prestige rotary pick, Remington Balder Pro head shaver, plus Series 9 Pro, Panasonic Arc5, Wahl Vanish, Remington F5) and beard trimmers (Philips Multigroom 9000/5000, Braun Series 9 13-in-1); Reviewed beard trimmers (Wahl Lithium Ion+, King C. Gillette PRO, Remington MB4700, Wahl Half Pint, Aqua Blade); NBC clipper picks (Wahl Elite Pro, Lithium Pro, Remington HC6550/HKVAC2000A, Oster Fast Feed); maker/retailer pages for Andis Master, Wahl Magic Clip, Oster Classic 76. CHOICE electric-shaver test page was retrieved but its Recommended labels are member-only; Consumer Reports was blocked and Which? not retrievable, so no winners from them are claimed. Dropped as SKU noise: Remington Limitless X7/X9 (kept as range), Remington 5-in-1 Titanium kit, Wahl Clip and Smooth, Complete Cut Pro, Designer Professional, Classic Edition, Color Trim Groomsman. No archetypes (tier shelf) and no craft traditions apply. Oster and King C. Gillette appear as makers without register entries (no brand page retrieved).",
